    "Actual Claude 2.1.269 acknowledged four peer/human/answer/peer inputs in order and produced four correlated replies under one provider record. History shows one ask_human tool result with only the posted ID, and one answer in a busy queued_command attachment with preserved reply_to.",
    "The first new transport capacity check used a compact MCP claimed field against the raw daemon Lease response. That driver failure and the corrected seven-scenario pass are both retained.",
    "The initial ad hoc provider-history parser missed busy input attachments. The corrected parser counts the provider-native attachment once and excludes enqueue/remove bookkeeping and rendered copies."
